From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kvmem): HIP/ROCm compat layer and CMake wiring; adapter
 compiles clean

Build wiring
- CMakeLists / src/CMakeLists: the LLAMA_KVMEM branch now covers GGML_HIP. On
  Windows the ROCm build takes ggml-hip's CXX_IS_HIPCC path (CMake on Windows has
  no HIP language), so the stage-in .cu is compiled as CXX with the ROCm clang++
  driver and llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h handles the CUDA -> HIP mapping.
  find_package(hip) is repeated here because hip::host / hip::device are
  directory-scoped IMPORTED targets and ggml-hip is a sibling directory.
- Non-Windows HIP and CPU-only builds fail loudly instead of mislinking.

Adapter ports
- src/adapter/llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h (new): 40 CUDA -> HIP name mappings,
  verified symbol by symbol against the ROCm 7.1 headers. __nv_bfloat16 maps to
  __hip_bfloat16 and half maps to __half, because AMD HIP provides neither
  CUDA spelling.
- llama-kvmem-stagein.cu, llama-kvmem-transfer.h, llama-memory-kvmem.cpp,
  llama-memory-kvmem-mtp.cpp: cuda_runtime.h / cuda_fp16.h / cuda_bf16.h routed
  through the shim.

PrismML divergence fixes
- llama-kv-cache: restore the trailing "const char * name_tag" parameter that the
  prism branch dropped. KVMem builds a second cache (llama-memory-kvmem-mtp.cpp
  passes "kvmem-mtp"), so the tensor names have to stay unique; naming is back to
  the upstream "cache_%sk_l%d" form with name_tag defaulting to "".

Verified: 10/10 kvmem objects compile with 0 errors against the PrismML tree
(5 adapter .cpp, llama-kvmem-stagein.cu.obj, 4 libkvmem host objects). Full link
not yet attempted.
---
 src/CMakeLists.txt                     | 27 +++++++++
 src/adapter/llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h  | 84 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/adapter/llama-kvmem-stagein.cu     |  4 ++
 src/adapter/llama-kvmem-transfer.h     |  4 ++
 src/adapter/llama-memory-kvmem-mtp.cpp |  4 ++
 src/adapter/llama-memory-kvmem.cpp     |  4 ++
 src/llama-kv-cache.cpp                 |  7 ++-
 src/llama-kv-cache.h                   | 12 ++--
 8 files changed, 138 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/adapter/llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 73ea0ba..73bd165 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,6 +80,33 @@ if (LLAMA_KVMEM)
         if (DEFINED CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES)
             set_property(TARGET llama PROPERTY CUDA_ARCHITECTURES ${CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES})
         endif()
+    elseif (GGML_HIP)
+        # KVMem's stage-in is CUDA source. On Windows the ROCm build takes the
+        # CXX_IS_HIPCC path (ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt: "CMake on Windows
+        # doesn't support the HIP language yet"), i.e. ggml compiles its
+        # ../ggml-cuda/*.cu as CXX and the ROCm clang++ driver puts .cu files into
+        # HIP mode by extension. Mirror exactly that: same compiler, same language,
+        # plus llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h for the CUDA -> HIP name mapping.
+        # A non-Windows HIP build would have to enable the HIP language at the
+        # project root; that is not a configuration llm-stack builds, so fail loudly
+        # instead of producing a confusing link error.
+        if (NOT WIN32)
+            message(FATAL_ERROR
+                "LLAMA_KVMEM=ON with GGML_HIP is only wired for Windows/ROCm builds")
+        endif()
+        set(_kvmem_stagein ${LLAMA_KVMEM_ROOT}/src/adapter/llama-kvmem-stagein.cu)
+        set_source_files_properties(${_kvmem_stagein} PROPERTIES LANGUAGE CXX)
+        target_sources(llama PRIVATE ${_kvmem_stagein})
+        target_compile_definitions(llama PRIVATE LLAMA_KVMEM_HIP=1)
+        # hip::host / hip::device are IMPORTED targets created by ggml-hip's
+        # find_package(hip), so they are not visible in this sibling directory.
+        # hip_DIR is already in the cache, so this resolves immediately.
+        find_package(hip REQUIRED)
+        target_link_libraries(llama PRIVATE hip::device hip::host)
+    else()
+        message(FATAL_ERROR
+            "LLAMA_KVMEM=ON requires a GPU backend: KVMem's tiered KV store is staged "
+            "in through the CUDA/HIP stage-in path. Configure with -DGGML_HIP=ON or -DGGML_CUDA=ON.")
     endif()
     target_include_directories(llama PRIVATE
         ${LLAMA_KVMEM_ROOT}/kvmem/include
diff --git a/src/adapter/llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h b/src/adapter/llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3c66cff
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/adapter/llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+#pragma once
+
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// HIP/ROCm compatibility shim for KVMem's CUDA-only GPU stage-in path.
+//
+// KVMem upstream (v0.16.0-rc3) targets CUDA: `llama-kvmem-stagein.cu` and
+// `llama-kvmem-transfer.h` are compiled only when GGML_CUDA is on. llm-stack
+// builds this tree with GGML_HIP=ON (gfx1030 / RX 6900 XT), so the CUDA
+// translation units would otherwise not be built and every `kvmem_stagein_*`
+// symbol referenced from llama-memory-kvmem.cpp would fail to link.
+//
+// The CUDA surface actually used by the adapter is a strict subset of HIP's
+// runtime API. Verified against the vendored sources:
+//   * no __shfl_*, no atomicAdd, no __ldg, no texture/surface objects
+//   * only 25 host-side runtime entry points, all with hip* counterparts
+//   * kernel syntax (<<<>>>, __global__, blockIdx/threadIdx/blockDim) is
+//     identical between CUDA and HIP, so no kernel body needs touching
+// Therefore a name mapping is sufficient — no source fork of the adapter.
+//
+// Included only when LLAMA_KVMEM_HIP is defined (set by src/CMakeLists.txt for
+// GGML_HIP builds). The mappings are deliberately confined to this header so
+// the `cuda*` spellings cannot leak into any other translation unit.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+#include <hip/hip_runtime.h>
+#include <hip/hip_fp16.h>
+#include <hip/hip_bf16.h>
+
+// --- bfloat16 -------------------------------------------------------------
+// CUDA: `__nv_bfloat16` (cuda_bf16.h). HIP/AMD: `__hip_bfloat16`
+// (hip_bfloat16 is not visible in every ROCm 7.1 translation unit).
+// `__bfloat162float` / `__float2bfloat16` already exist in amd_hip_bf16.h.
+using __nv_bfloat16 = __hip_bfloat16;
+
+// --- fp16 -----------------------------------------------------------------
+// CUDA provides `half` as a synonym for `__half`; HIP does not.
+using half = __half;
+
+// --- runtime API types and enums -----------------------------------------
+#define cudaError_t              hipError_t
+#define cudaSuccess              hipSuccess
+#define cudaMemcpyKind           hipMemcpyKind
+#define cudaMemcpyHostToDevice   hipMemcpyHostToDevice
+#define cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost   hipMemcpyDeviceToHost
+#define cudaMemcpyDeviceToDevice hipMemcpyDeviceToDevice
+#define cudaStream_t             hipStream_t
+#define cudaEvent_t              hipEvent_t
+
+// --- runtime API functions ------------------------------------------------
+#define cudaGetErrorString       hipGetErrorString
+#define cudaGetLastError         hipGetLastError
+#define cudaStreamSynchronize    hipStreamSynchronize
+#define cudaEventCreateWithFlags hipEventCreateWithFlags
+#define cudaEventDisableTiming   hipEventDisableTiming
+#define cudaEventRecord          hipEventRecord
+#define cudaEventSynchronize     hipEventSynchronize
+#define cudaEventDestroy         hipEventDestroy
+#define cudaMalloc               hipMalloc
+#define cudaMallocHost           hipHostMalloc
+#define cudaFree                 hipFree
+#define cudaFreeHost             hipHostFree
+#define cudaMemcpy               hipMemcpy
+#define cudaMemcpyAsync          hipMemcpyAsync
+#define cudaMemsetAsync          hipMemsetAsync
+
+// --- device / stream management -------------------------------------------
+#define cudaSetDevice            hipSetDevice
+#define cudaGetDevice            hipGetDevice
+#define cudaDeviceSynchronize    hipDeviceSynchronize
+#define cudaStreamCreateWithFlags hipStreamCreateWithFlags
+#define cudaStreamNonBlocking    hipStreamNonBlocking
+#define cudaStreamDestroy        hipStreamDestroy
+#define cudaStreamWaitEvent      hipStreamWaitEvent
+
+// --- pointer attributes ---------------------------------------------------
+// CUDA spells the struct `cudaPointerAttributes`; HIP spells it
+// `hipPointerAttribute_t` (singular "Attribute"). The field names differ too,
+// but the vendored code only reads .type / .device, which both provide.
+#define cudaPointerAttributes    hipPointerAttribute_t
+#define cudaPointerGetAttributes hipPointerGetAttributes
+
+// hipStreamPerThread is a macro in hip_runtime_api.h; alias it explicitly so
+// the CUDA spelling keeps working.
+#define cudaStreamPerThread      hipStreamPerThread
